course: dictionary
lesson: 10951
title: Words for people at work
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A waitress is a woman or girl who works in a café or restaurant. Her job is to bring food and drinks to the tables and to take your order, which means writing down what you want to eat and drink.
explain: The word ends in -ess, which shows it is a woman or girl doing the job. Many places now use «server» or «waiting staff» for everyone who serves customers, so you may hear those words too.
explain: Context helps here: «And sometimes the gossip is lovely, like a big kind tip for a waitress.» A tip is extra money given to say thank you for good service. So a big kind tip is a generous way of thanking her. You can check it by swapping in your meaning: it still makes sense.
fact: A waitress is a woman or girl whose job is to bring food and drinks to customers' tables in a café or restaurant.
fact: A waitress takes your order, which means she writes down what you want to eat and drink.
fact: «Waitress» is a noun, and its plural is «waitresses».
fact: Many places now say «server» or «waiting staff» for everyone who serves customers.
fact: Useful phrases: «work as a waitress», «call the waitress», «tip the waitress».
exercise: «She works as a waitress at the café by the station.» What is a waitress? | A person who sells tickets on a train | *A person whose job is to bring food and drinks to customers' tables | A person who cooks the food in a kitchen | A person who cleans the café floors
exercise: Write the plural of waitress. | waitress | *waitresses | waiters | waitressis
exercise: «...like a big kind tip for a waitress.» What does a tip for a waitress mean? | *Extra money given to say thank you for good service | A complaint about the food | A bill for the meal | A menu of drinks
test: Which phrase means to give extra money to a waitress to say thank you? | call the waitress | ask the waitress for the menu | *tip the waitress | work as a waitress
test: What does a waitress take at your table? | *your order | a bus ticket | a map of the town | a bath
exam: In «a big kind tip for a waitress», what is the tip? | A plate of food | A fork and spoon | *Money given to thank the waitress | A bill for the meal
